Git Commit Message Generation Rules

When generating a Git commit message using the Source Control (SCM) AI button, you MUST strictly adhere to the following logic and format. No exceptions are allowed.

Context & Scope Analysis (CRITICAL):
1. Target Staged Changes First: analyze ONLY currently staged changes. Ignore unstaged files if staged files exist.
2. Fallback: if and only if there are NO staged changes, analyze all pending changes.
3. Base the message strictly on the actual code diff — do not hallucinate features.

Format Structure:
- A single Conventional Commit title (e.g. feat(text): …, fix(phone): …, chore(release): …).
- A single mandatory blank line.
- A detailed bulleted list of technical what + why.
- End with a blank line and exactly:
  Co-Authored-By: Mohammed El Shora <riyadm2001@gmail.com>

Constraints:
- Output ONLY the commit message — no conversational wrapper.
- Title under 72 characters, imperative mood, present tense.
- Focus on architectural intent and the problem solved.
